Primary-assembly composition correction (2026-11-07)
- Ensembl Release 112 README states that primary assembly contains all top-level sequence regions excluding haplotypes and patches.
- The official `Homo_sapiens.GRCh38.dna.nonchromosomal.fa.gz` file is therefore a required primary-assembly component; it contains unassigned/nonchromosomal top-level sequences and must not be omitted.
- Assembly inventory for GCA_000001405.29 reports 194 primary top-level sequences: 25 chromosome sequences plus 169 scaffold/nonchromosomal sequences, total 3,099,750,718 bp; scaffold/nonchromosomal total 11,464,317 bp.
- ALT, patch, haplotype files and `dna.toplevel.fa.gz` are excluded from the primary-assembly plan.
- Manifest updated to include the nonchromosomal official URL. No large download, merge, or HISAT2 operation was performed in this step.

